
========================================================================
  KRAWTCHOUK POLYNOMIALS vs H(T) -- TILING HYPERCUBE ANALYSIS
========================================================================

Krawtchouk polynomials K_k(x; m) on the binary Hamming scheme Q_m
K_k(x; m) = sum_{j=0}^{k} (-1)^j C(x,j) C(m-x, k-j)

Tiling: m = C(n-1, 2) bits, each bit = one non-base-path arc direction
Hamming weight x = number of 1-bits in the tiling

Sanity check: K_1(x; 6) for x=0..6:
  K_1(0; 6) = 6  [expect 6 - 2*0 = 6]
  K_1(1; 6) = 4  [expect 6 - 2*1 = 4]
  K_1(2; 6) = 2  [expect 6 - 2*2 = 2]
  K_1(3; 6) = 0  [expect 6 - 2*3 = 0]
  K_1(4; 6) = -2  [expect 6 - 2*4 = -2]
  K_1(5; 6) = -4  [expect 6 - 2*5 = -4]
  K_1(6; 6) = -6  [expect 6 - 2*6 = -6]


